  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1106 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nRiver flooding continues along the Big Blue and Turkey Creek, with \nthe crest beginning to move out of Beatrice. Most gages are expected \nto drop below flood stage by Monday night. \n\nIt was a another beautiful, dry day as high pressured remained over \nthe region. A quick glance at visible satellite revealed a few wisps \nof clouds over the forecast area this afternoon, otherwise sunny \nskies prevailed. Temperatures once again pushed into the mid 70s by \nlate afternoon. \n\nMostly sunny conditions will prevail over the next several days, \nwith highs reaching at least the 70s through next week. A thermal \nridge over the western CONUS will shift eastward Tuesday, warming us \na few extra degrees, into the low 80s. While there is still a \nslight chance for a few warm air advection showers Thursday into\nFriday, the overall forecast remains dry through at least next \nweekend. \n\nLonger range models are beginning to hint at a potent upper level \ntrough digging through the western CONUS late next weekend. If this \noccurs, we can expect notable warming ahead of this system, \nwith a chance for showers and storms, followed by cooler \ntemperatures as the storm system moves through. But again, \nthat's looking pretty far into the future where forecast details\nare still quite uncertain.",
